Author:     Brendan Abolivier <brendan@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Thu Jul 3 09:39:26 2025 -0700
Commit:     Brendan Abolivier <brendan@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Thu Jul 3 09:39:26 2025 -0700

    Bug 1971540 - Part 2: Handle EWS authentication failures. r=edicharry


    Although most of the error handling for EWS had been architectured around
    happening inside the C++ callbacks, I realised this simply cannot work for
    authentication errors as we'll want to retry the request with a different
    authentication header in some cases (e.g. when a new password is entered). As a
    result, this patch reworks the handling of authentication errors to be done in
    Rust, closer to the code that generates and sends requests.

    As a side-effect, I ended up rewriting a bunch of the existing alerting code
    from `nsImapIncomingServer` in Rust for convenience, while also exposing the
    new code over FFI so the C++ IMAP implementation can eventually start using it.

    I've intentionally descoped removing the `IEwsClient::Error` enum (and
    associated processing via the `process_error_with_cb*` functions) from this
    patch, since this requires updating a lot of callback classes which would
    unnecessarily bloat this already large patch. I'll take care of this in a part
    3.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D255652

